# Local d45 → navigation candidate diagnostic, 2026-09-27

The repository's unchanged `compare_performance.py` was run offline against the one local complex-UI receipt for each x64 configuration in `profiles-d45` and `profiles-navigation-final`. The fixture matches (`dxui-complex-ui-v2`, benchmark SHA `B1081AA75BF0EB30B330F835415225C5242B6629FEECDF597B06BACFAB197D0B`, 1280×720/96 DPI, five 40-frame rounds). The final local receipts identify d45 as `sourceCommit` with `sourceDirty:true`: these were captured before the optimization was committed. Its captured `DxUi.Accessibility.cpp` and `DxUiTests.Menu.cpp` SHA-256 values do match the later clean 73ba checkout, but the run receipt is still pre-commit/dirty. Treat this as a diagnostic comparison, not an exact-73ba source qualification or a stable regression/waiver. The raw comparator reports and logs are preserved alongside this note.

| Configuration | Comparator | Clean frame P50 / P95 ms | Dirty frame P50 / P95 ms | Changed flagged median |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Release | advice-required | 0.3900→0.3684 / 0.4361→0.4551 | 1.7768→1.7411 / 2.0732→2.0412 | dirty compose CPU P95 0.0178→0.0351 ms (+97.19%) |
| Debug | within-noise-budget | 0.4207→0.3917 / 0.4869→0.4888 | 2.3348→2.3724 / 3.1238→2.8316 | none |
| ASan Debug | advice-required | 0.4085→0.4205 / 0.4964→0.5535 | 10.0709→9.7276 / 12.3929→11.7228 | clean frame P95 +11.50%, prepare P95 0.0011→0.0012 ms (+9.09%), compose CPU P95 0.0155→0.0169 ms (+9.03%) |

Every clean 40-frame round reports zero C++ allocations; every composition reports zero allocations. Dirty allocation medians are unchanged: 2,160 per Release round and 10,280 per Debug/ASan round. Surface and replacement peaks remain 3,686,400 bytes in every round; hidden preparations/compositions remain zero. These are offscreen completed WARP frames, not presented FPS. The previously accepted menu timing envelope applies to earlier recorded menu measurements, not these new common-fixture flags.

The changed accessibility snapshot builder is **not reached by this benchmark**. `ComplexUiBenchmark::Run` builds `ComplexUiScene` and times `view.Prepare`/`view.Composite` (`Tests/Embedded/ComplexUiBenchmark.h`, lines 91–113 and 155–191). `ComplexUiScene::Initialize` attaches an `EmbeddedHost` and sets the root, with no `AttachAccessibility` or `UpdateAccessibility` call (`Samples/ComplexUi/ComplexUiScene.h`, lines 61–92). `ControlHost::SetRoot` asks for `RefreshWindowHostAccessibilitySnapshot` (`src/Controls/DxUi.WindowHost.cpp`, lines 1341–1358), but this returns immediately when the embedded host has no HWND (`src/Controls/DxUi.Accessibility.cpp`, lines 8427–8433). Embedded snapshot publication requires an explicit `AttachAccessibility`/`UpdateAccessibility` target (`DxUi.Accessibility.cpp`, lines 8698–8758). Thus these common-fixture flags cannot isolate the changed builder's cost; same-variant ABBA controls already showed timing movement in the unchanged common workload. Preserve the flags as emitted, without attributing them to the builder.

The ordinary-menu resource fixture **is** present in each final local MenuAccessibility log: 24 samples each (12 and 128 rows × four cycles × before/open/closed) at 476×322 px/96 DPI, with exact UIA child counts 12 and 128. Release warm-cycle open-minus-before process-heap busy bytes are 273,106→273,206 at 12 rows and 627,673→619,450 at 128 rows versus local d45; 128-row closed-minus-before is 41,327→41,500 bytes. The final 12/128 values are near the candidate C1/C2 ABBA values (about 272,211/628,753 B) and do not show added live-heap growth from the navigation optimization in this short fixture. The ASan heap walker reports zero busy-byte deltas, so its heap figures are unavailable for this comparison; its child, geometry and process observations remain recorded. `resource-sample-summary.json` retains the six configuration summaries and per-cycle deltas.

The smallest next evidence is the already running exact-73ba six-profile CI. It directly exercises the 4,096-row Menu/menus-accessibility bounds and yields clean-source complex-UI receipts. Compare those receipts against exact-d45 CI per configuration only after completion. A further common-WARP rerun is justified only if that independent pair repeats a directional flag and there is a specific timing question to isolate; running more noisy local rounds now would not establish changed-builder causality.
